(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast the structural architectures, monomer subunits, nucleotide dependencies, and polarities of Microfilaments, Microtubules, and Intermediate Filaments.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The eukaryotic cytoskeleton comprises three distinct filamentous polymer networks:) Tj
T*
(   1. Microfilaments \(F-Actin\):) Tj
T*
(   - Monomer Subunit: Globular G-Actin \(42 kDa\).) Tj
T*
(   - Polymer Structure: Two parallel protofilaments twisting around each other in a right-handed) Tj
T*
(   double helix with a 7 nm diameter and 36 nm pitch.) Tj
T*
(   - Nucleotide Binding: Binds and hydrolyzes ATP.) Tj
T*
(   - Polarity: Distinct structural polarity; possesses a fast-growing barbed \(+\) end and) Tj
T*
(   slow-growing pointed \(-\) end.) Tj
T*
(   2. Microtubules:) Tj
T*
(   - Monomer Subunit: Heterodimer of alpha- and beta-tubulin \(55 kDa each; 110 kDa dimer\).) Tj
T*
(   - Polymer Structure: Hollow, rigid cylinder with an outer diameter of 25 nm and inner lumen of) Tj
T*
(   14 nm, typically composed of 13 parallel protofilaments.) Tj
T*
(   - Nucleotide Binding: Alpha-tubulin binds GTP non-exchangeably \(N-site\); beta-tubulin binds and) Tj
T*
(   hydrolyzes GTP \(E-site\).) Tj
T*
(   - Polarity: Inherently polar; terminating with exposed beta-subunits at the plus \(+\) end and) Tj
T*
(   alpha-subunits at the minus \(-\) end.) Tj
T*
(   3. Intermediate Filaments \(IFs\):) Tj
T*
(   - Monomer Subunit: Diverse tissue-specific proteins \(Keratins, Vimentin, Desmin,) Tj
T*
(   Neurofilaments, Lamins\) sharing an alpha-helical central rod domain \(~310-350 amino acids\).) Tj
T*
(   - Polymer Structure: 10-12 nm flexible, rope-like polymers formed by lateral association of 8) Tj
T*
(   protofibrils \(32 individual polypeptide chains per cross-section\).) Tj
T*
(   - Nucleotide Binding: Do NOT bind or hydrolyze nucleotides \(ATP/GTP-independent assembly\).) Tj
T*
(   - Polarity: Non-polar! Two parallel dimers associate in an antiparallel, staggered manner to) Tj
T*
(   form a symmetrical tetramer, abolishing directional polarity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the molecular mechanism of Microtubule Dynamic Instability and detail the structural role of the GTP cap.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Dynamic Instability of Microtubules \(Mitchison and Kirschner Paradigm\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition: Dynamic instability is the coexistence of growing and shrinking microtubule ends) Tj
T*
(   within the same cellular population, characterized by stochastic transitions between prolonged) Tj
T*
(   growth \(polymerization\) and rapid shrinkage \(depolymerization\).) Tj
T*
(   2. The GTP Cap Hypothesis:) Tj
T*
(   - Free alpha-beta tubulin heterodimers have GTP bound to the beta-tubulin exchangeable site.) Tj
T*
(   - As dimers add to the growing plus-end, they form straight protofilaments that pack stably) Tj
T*
(   into the cylindrical lattice.) Tj
T*
(   - Shortly after incorporation, beta-tubulin hydrolyzes its bound GTP to GDP, releasing) Tj
T*
(   inorganic phosphate \(Pi\). The resulting GDP-tubulin subunit adopts a curved, strained) Tj
T*
(   conformation \(bent by ~12 degrees\).) Tj
T*
(   - However, as long as the rate of dimer addition exceeds the rate of GTP hydrolysis, a) Tj
T*
(   protective layer of GTP-bound tubulin subunits \(the GTP Cap\) remains at the extreme plus-end,) Tj
T*
(   mechanically constraining the internal GDP-tubulin lattice in a straight configuration.) Tj
T*
(   3. Catastrophe and Rescue Transitions:) Tj
T*
(   - Catastrophe: If growth slows and GTP hydrolysis catches up to the tip, the protective GTP cap) Tj
T*
(   is lost. The strained GDP-tubulin protofilaments spring outward, peeling back like curved) Tj
T*
(   banana peels. Rapid protofilament depolymerization ensues at rates up to 30 microns/minute.) Tj
T*
ET

