(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the structural organization of Sarcomeres and detail the regulatory roles of the Troponin-Tropomyosin complex in excitation-contraction coupling.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Sarcomere Architecture and Troponin-Tropomyosin Regulation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Sarcomere Structural Organization:) Tj
T*
(   The sarcomere is the fundamental contractile unit of striated muscle, bounded by two Z-discs:) Tj
T*
(   - A-Band \(Anisotropic\): Central dark band containing thick myosin filaments overlapping with) Tj
T*
(   thin filaments; remains constant in length during contraction.) Tj
T*
(   - I-Band \(Isotropic\): Light band containing only thin actin filaments; shortens during) Tj
T*
(   contraction.) Tj
T*
(   - H-Zone: Central region of A-band containing only thick filaments \(lacks actin\); narrows or) Tj
T*
(   disappears during full contraction.) Tj
T*
(   - M-Line: Central structural anchor holding thick filaments in a hexagonal array.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Troponin-Tropomyosin Steric Blocking Model \(Huxley-Hanson\):) Tj
T*
(   - Tropomyosin: An alpha-helical coiled-coil dimer polymerizing head-to-tail along the groove of) Tj
T*
(   F-actin, spanning 7 actin monomers.) Tj
T*
(   - Troponin Complex: Positioned at 38.5 nm intervals along tropomyosin, consisting of three) Tj
T*
(   subunits:) Tj
T*
(   - Troponin T \(TnT\): Anchors the troponin complex to tropomyosin.) Tj
T*
(   - Troponin I \(TnI\): Inhibitory subunit that binds actin, holding tropomyosin in a position that) Tj
T*
(   sterically blocks myosin-binding sites \(Blocked State\).) Tj
T*
(   - Troponin C \(TnC\): Calcium-binding sensor homologous to calmodulin, possessing four EF-hand) Tj
T*
(   motifs \(two high-affinity structural sites, two low-affinity regulatory sites\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Calcium-Mediated Activation:) Tj
T*
(   Action potential propagation down T-tubules activates DHPR-RyR1 coupling, flooding the) Tj
T*
(   sarcoplasm with Ca2+ \(rising from 0.1 microM to 10 microM\). Ca2+ binds to the regulatory) Tj
T*
(   low-affinity sites of TnC, inducing an allosteric conformational shift that pulls TnI away from) Tj
T*
(   actin. Tropomyosin rolls 25 degrees deeper into the actin groove, unmasking myosin-binding) Tj
T*
(   sites and initiating forceful cross-bridge cycling.) Tj
T*
