(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structural mechanics of Clathrin-coated vesicle formation, contrasting the roles of AP-2 adaptors, Clathrin triskelions, and Dynamin GTPase.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Biomechanical Stages of Clathrin-Coated Vesicle Formation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Nucleation and Cargo Selection \(AP-2 Adaptor\):) Tj
T*
(   - The plasma-membrane-specific adaptor complex AP-2 \(alpha, beta-2, mu-2, sigma-2\) exists in an) Tj
T*
(   auto-inhibited closed state in the cytosol.) Tj
T*
(   - Coincident binding to PI\(4,5\)P2 on the inner plasma membrane leaflet and cargo motifs) Tj
T*
(   \(tyrosine-based YXXPhi motif binding to mu-2; dileucine motif binding to beta-2\) triggers an) Tj
T*
(   open active conformation.) Tj
T*
(   - The beta-2 subunit appendage recruits clathrin triskelions from the cytoplasm.) Tj
T*
(   2. Lattice Assembly and Membrane Curvature \(Clathrin Triskelions\):) Tj
T*
(   - Clathrin triskelions \(three 190 kDa heavy chains and three 25 kDa light chains\) self-assemble) Tj
T*
(   into a geodesic polyhedral cage consisting of 12 pentagons and variable hexagons.) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanical rigidity of the growing lattice forces the flexible phospholipid bilayer to curve) Tj
T*
(   inward, forming a deeply invaginated clathrin-coated pit.) Tj
T*
(   3. Constriction and Scission \(Dynamin GTPase\):) Tj
T*
(   - As the coated pit deepens, its neck narrows. Dynamin, a large 100 kDa GTPase, is recruited to) Tj
T*
(   the neck via its pleckstrin homology \(PH\) domain binding to PI\(4,5\)P2 and its PRD domain) Tj
T*
(   binding to amphiphysin/endophilin.) Tj
T*
(   - Dynamin polymerizes into a helical collar surrounding the constricted membrane neck.) Tj
T*
(   - Upon concerted GTP hydrolysis, dynamin undergoes a rapid conformational constriction and) Tj
T*
(   torsional twist that squeezes the lipid neck to a radius < 1.5 nm, inducing hemi-fission and) Tj
T*
(   scission of the budded transport vesicle.) Tj
T*
(   4. Uncoating and Disassembly:) Tj
T*
(   - Synaptojanin \(a lipid 5-phosphatase\) dephosphorylates PI\(4,5\)P2 to PI\(4\)P, destabilizing AP-2) Tj
T*
(   membrane binding.) Tj
T*
