(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the core components and biochemical steps of the ESCRT machinery in multivesicular body \(MVB\) sorting.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The ESCRT Machinery in Multivesicular Body \(MVB\) Biogenesis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physiological Role:) Tj
T*
(   Downregulation of activated cell surface signaling receptors \(e.g., EGFR\) requires their) Tj
T*
(   internalization and physical sequestration inside intraluminal vesicles \(ILVs\) of late) Tj
T*
(   endosomes \(multivesicular bodies\), targeting them for destruction upon lysosomal fusion.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Four Sequential ESCRT Complexes:) Tj
T*
(   - ESCRT-0 \(HRS - STAM\): Ubiquitin-tagged cargo receptors are recognized on the endosomal) Tj
T*
(   membrane by ESCRT-0 via tandem ubiquitin-interacting motifs \(UIMs\). HRS binds PI\(3\)P,) Tj
T*
(   concentrating ubiquitinated receptors into microdomains.) Tj
T*
(   - ESCRT-I \(TSG101 - VPS28 - VPS37 - MVB12\): Recruited by direct interaction between HRS and) Tj
T*
(   TSG101 \(a ubiquitin E2-variant\). ESCRT-I passes cargo to ESCRT-II.) Tj
T*
(   - ESCRT-II \(VPS22 - VPS25 - VPS36\): Contains a GLUE domain binding PI\(3\)P and ubiquitin. VPS25) Tj
T*
(   subunits nucleate polymerization of the downstream ESCRT-III machinery.) Tj
T*
(   - ESCRT-III \(CHMP6 - CHMP4 - CHMP2 - CHMP3\): Small cytosolic monomers that assemble into) Tj
T*
(   high-order spiral polymers on the endosomal membrane. Unlike clathrin, ESCRT-III lines the) Tj
T*
(   inside of the budding neck, pulling membrane away from the cytoplasm into the endosome lumen.) Tj
T*
(   3. Membrane Scission and Vps4-Mediated Disassembly:) Tj
T*
(   Constriction of the ESCRT-III spiral drives membrane scission from within the neck, pinching) Tj
T*
(   off an intraluminal vesicle containing the receptor.) Tj
T*
(   Finally, the hexameric AAA+ ATPase Vps4 binds ESCRT-III subunits, hydrolyzing ATP to) Tj
T*
(   disassemble the polymers back into soluble monomers for reuse.) Tj
