(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the molecular architecture of the 9+2 Axoneme in motile cilia and explain how sliding of outer doublets is converted into bending.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Ultrastructure and Mechanobiology of the Motile Axoneme:) Tj
T*
(   1. The 9+2 Ultrastructural Arrangement:) Tj
T*
(   Motile cilia and eukaryotic flagella \(e.g., sperm tail, respiratory epithelia\) possess a) Tj
T*
(   canonical 9+2 axoneme:) Tj
T*
(   - Nine Outer Doublet Microtubules: Each doublet consists of a complete A-tubule \(13) Tj
T*
(   protofilaments\) fused to an incomplete B-tubule \(10 protofilaments\).) Tj
T*
(   - Central Pair: Two central singlet microtubules \(13 protofilaments each\) surrounded by a) Tj
T*
(   central sheath.) Tj
T*
(   - Radial Spokes: Structural protein projections extending from each outer A-tubule toward the) Tj
T*
(   central sheath, transmitting mechanochemical signals.) Tj
T*
(   - Nexin Links \(Nexin-Dynein Regulatory Complex - N-DRC\): Interdoublet elastic protein bridges) Tj
T*
(   connecting adjacent doublets, maintaining structural alignment.) Tj
T*
(   2. Axonemal Dynein Motors:) Tj
T*
(   Attached to each A-tubule are multi-headed axonemal dynein complexes: Outer Dynein Arms \(ODAs,) Tj
T*
(   regulating beat frequency\) and Inner Dynein Arms \(IDAs, regulating waveform amplitude\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Conversion of Microtubule Sliding to Waveform Bending \(Satir Model\):) Tj
T*
(   - In isolated doublets without structural constraints, ATP addition causes dynein motors to) Tj
T*
(   walk processively along the adjacent B-tubule toward the minus-end, causing unrestrained) Tj
T*
(   parallel sliding.) Tj
T*
