(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the pathophysiology of Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia \(Kartagener Syndrome\) and its link to situs inversus.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia \(PCD\) and Kartagener Syndrome Pathophysiology:) Tj
T*
(   1. Genetic Etiology:) Tj
T*
(   Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia is a genetically heterogeneous autosomal recessive disorder caused) Tj
T*
(   by loss-of-function mutations in genes encoding structural components of the motile axoneme,) Tj
T*
(   most commonly:) Tj
T*
(   - DNAH5 and DNAI1 \(encoding heavy and intermediate chains of outer dynein arms\).) Tj
T*
(   - DNAL1 \(light chain of ODAs\).) Tj
T*
(   - CCDC39 and CCDC40 \(nexin-dynein regulatory complex\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Clinical Manifestations:) Tj
T*
(   - Respiratory System: Chronic sinusitis, recurrent otitis media, and severe bronchiectasis due) Tj
T*
(   to paralysis of the mucociliary escalator in tracheal and bronchial epithelia.) Tj
T*
(   - Reproductive System: Male infertility due to immotile sperm flagella; reduced female) Tj
T*
(   fertility due to defective ciliary transport in fallopian tubes.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Molecular Basis of Situs Inversus \(Kartagener Triad\):) Tj
T*
(   Kartagener syndrome presents with the classic triad of bronchiectasis, chronic sinusitis, and) Tj
T*
(   situs inversus totalis \(complete mirror-image reversal of thoracic and abdominal organs\):) Tj
T*
(   - During early embryonic gastrulation, a specialized transient depression called the embryonic) Tj
T*
(   node possesses motile monocilia with a 9+0 architecture.) Tj
T*
(   - In healthy embryos, coordinated clockwise rotation of nodal cilia generates a directional) Tj
T*
(   leftward fluid flow across the node \('nodal flow'\).) Tj
T*
(   - This leftward hydrodynamic flow transports signaling morphogens \(Nodal, Lefty2\) or bends) Tj
T*
(   immotile sensory cilia on the left margin, activating the transcription factor Pitx2) Tj
T*
(   exclusively on the left side of the lateral plate mesoderm.) Tj
T*
(   - In PCD patients, paralyzed nodal cilia eliminate leftward flow. Left-right asymmetric) Tj
T*
(   signaling is left to pure random chance, resulting in 50% of affected individuals developing) Tj
T*
(   complete situs inversus.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
