(   intracellular actin cytoskeleton:) Tj
T*
(   - Transmembrane Core: Integrin alpha-beta heterodimers \(e.g., alpha-5-beta-1 binding) Tj
T*
(   fibronectin\).) Tj
T*
(   - Core Structural Adaptors: Talin and Vinculin directly linking integrin beta-tails to F-actin.) Tj
T*
(   - Enzymatic & Signaling Kinases: Focal Adhesion Kinase \(FAK\), Src kinase, Paxillin.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mechanotransduction Mechanism \(Talin-Vinculin Spring\):) Tj
T*
(   - Intracellular actomyosin contractility \(mediated by non-muscle myosin II pulling on actin) Tj
T*
(   stress fibers\) exerts mechanical tension on talin.) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanical stretching of talin unfolds its hidden rod domains, exposing cryptic binding sites) Tj
T*
(   for Vinculin.) Tj
T*
(   - Vinculin recruitment stabilizes the linkage, crosslinking additional actin filaments into) Tj
T*
(   thick, bundled contractile stress fibers.) Tj
T*
(   - Concurrently, mechanical stretch induces FAK auto-phosphorylation at Tyr-397, creating a) Tj
T*
(   high-affinity binding site for the SH2 domain of Src kinase.) Tj
T*
(   - Active FAK-Src complex phosphorylates downstream substrates \(paxillin, p130Cas\), activating) Tj
T*
(   Rac1 and RhoA signaling pathways that govern cell spreading, survival \(suppression of anoikis\),) Tj
T*
(   and directional durotaxis \(migration toward stiffer substrate matrices\).) Tj
