(   [Problem Statement]: Explain how the Kinesin-5 \(Eg5\) motor operates during mitosis to establish bipolar mitotic spindle architecture.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Kinesin-5 \(Eg5 / Kif11\) Mechanics in Bipolar Spindle Assembly:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Kinesin-5 is a homotetrameric kinesin family member organized as a bipolar dumbbell:) Tj
T*
(   - Two pairs of catalytic motor heads are located at opposite ends of an extended central) Tj
T*
(   coiled-coil antiparallel stalk.) Tj
T*
(   - Both pairs of motor heads are plus-end-directed microtubule motors.) Tj
T*
(   2. Crosslinking and Sliding of Antiparallel Microtubules:) Tj
T*
(   During prophase and prometaphase, duplicated centrosomes must separate to opposite sides of the) Tj
T*
(   nucleus:) Tj
T*
(   - Kinesin-5 binds simultaneously to two overlapping, antiparallel polar microtubules emanating) Tj
T*
(   from opposing centrosomes.) Tj
T*
(   - Because both sets of motor heads walk toward the plus-ends of their respective microtubules,) Tj
T*
(   the two antiparallel microtubules are driven in opposite directions \(sliding outward\).) Tj
T*
(   - This mutual push forces the two centrosomes \(spindle poles\) apart, establishing the bipolar) Tj
T*
(   mitotic spindle.) Tj
T*
(   3. Pharmacological Inhibition \(Monastrol\):) Tj
T*
(   - Monastrol is an allosteric small-molecule inhibitor that binds an induced-fit pocket on the) Tj
T*
(   Eg5 motor domain, trapping it in an ADP-bound state.) Tj
T*
(   - Inhibited Eg5 cannot generate sliding force. Antagonistic minus-end dynein motors pull) Tj
T*
(   spindle poles together, arresting cells in a characteristic 'monoastral' \(rosette-like\) spindle) Tj
T*
(   configuration, triggering the spindle assembly checkpoint \(SAC\) and mitotic apoptosis.) Tj
T*
