(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the functional role of the Retromer complex in endosome-to-Golgi retrograde transport and its clinical significance in Alzheimer's disease.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Retromer Complex Architecture and Alzheimer's Disease Pathogenesis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Molecular Architecture of Retromer:) Tj
T*
(   Retromer is a conserved multi-protein coat complex that orchestrates retrograde trafficking of) Tj
T*
(   specific transmembrane receptors from early/late endosomes back to the Trans-Golgi Network) Tj
T*
(   \(TGN\):) Tj
T*
(   - Cargo-Selective Trimer \(Vps26 - Vps29 - Vps35\): Vps35 acts as a central scaffold binding) Tj
T*
(   cargo cytosolic tails; Vps26 binds sorting motifs; Vps29 binds regulatory proteins.) Tj
T*
(   - Membrane-Deforming Dimer: Sorting Nexins \(SNX1, SNX2, SNX5, SNX6\) possessing PX domains) Tj
T*
(   \(binding PI\(3\)P on endosomes\) and BAR domains that sense and stabilize membrane tubulation.) Tj
T*
(   2. Primary Physiological Cargoes:) Tj
T*
(   - Cation-Independent Mannose-6-Phosphate Receptor \(CI-MPR\): Retrieves empty receptors from) Tj
T*
(   endosomes to TGN for further rounds of lysosomal enzyme sorting.) Tj
T*
(   - Wntless \(Wls\): Recycles Wntless for sustained Wnt ligand secretion.) Tj
T*
(   - SorLA \(Sorting-related receptor with A-type repeats\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Pathological Connection to Alzheimer's Disease:) Tj
T*
(   - Amyloid Precursor Protein \(APP\) is cleaved by beta-secretase \(BACE1\) within acidic endosomes) Tj
T*
(   to generate neurotoxic Amyloid-beta \(A-beta\) peptides.) Tj
T*
(   - Retromer binds SorLA to rapidly clear APP out of endosomes back to the TGN, shielding it from) Tj
T*
(   BACE1 cleavage.) Tj
T*
(   - In sporadic Alzheimer's disease, mutations in VPS35 \(p.Asp620Asn\) or transcriptional) Tj
T*
(   downregulation of retromer components trap APP inside endosomes, markedly increasing A-beta-42) Tj
T*
(   production, amyloid plaque deposition, and neurodegeneration.) Tj
T*
