(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the molecular mechanism of Caveolae formation and their physiological functions in endothelial mechanosensing and endocytosis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Caveolae Ultrastructure, Biogenesis, and Functions:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Caveolae \('little caves'\) are flask-shaped, 50-100 nm invaginations of the plasma membrane) Tj
T*
(   abundant in endothelial cells, adipocytes, and smooth muscle:) Tj
T*
(   - Caveolins \(Cav1, Cav2, Cav3\): Integral hairpin membrane proteins with both N- and C-termini) Tj
T*
(   facing the cytoplasm and a central hydrophobic intramembrane domain inserting into the inner) Tj
T*
(   leaflet.) Tj
T*
(   - Cavins \(Cavin-1 to Cavin-4\): Soluble peripheral proteins oligomerizing into a striated) Tj
T*
(   polyhedral coat over the bulbous caveolin membrane surface. Cavin-1 \(PTRF\) is strictly) Tj
T*
(   essential for caveolar morphology.) Tj
T*
(   - Lipid Composition: Highly enriched in cholesterol and sphingomyelin, forming a specialized,) Tj
T*
(   immobile liquid-ordered microdomain.) Tj
T*
(   2. Physiological Functions:) Tj
T*
(   - Endothelial Transcytosis: Facilitates non-clathrin-dependent uptake and transport of) Tj
T*
(   macromolecules \(serum albumin, LDL, insulin\) across vascular endothelial barriers via) Tj
T*
(   Cav1-dependent budding.) Tj
T*
(   - Mechanical Buffer / Shear Stress Reservoir: In response to sudden hemodynamic pressure or) Tj
T*
(   mechanical cell stretch, caveolae rapidly flatten into the plane of the plasma membrane without) Tj
T*
(   breaking, buffering membrane tension and preventing membrane rupture.) Tj
T*
(   - Signal Transduction Platform: Scaffolds endothelial nitric oxide synthase \(eNOS\), receptor) Tj
T*
(   tyrosine kinases, and G-protein subunits within its scaffolding domain \(CSD\), regulating nitric) Tj
T*
(   oxide production in response to laminar blood flow.) Tj
