(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the architecture and mechanochemical cycle of Cytoplasmic Dynein, and detail how Dynactin and Lis1 regulate its processivity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Cytoplasmic Dynein Structure, Power Stroke, and Dynactin-Lis1 Regulation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Cytoplasmic Dynein-1 is a massive 1.4 MDa multi-subunit retrograde microtubule motor:) Tj
T*
(   - Two Heavy Chains \(HC\): Each heavy chain contains a C-terminal planar ring of six AAA+ modules) Tj
T*
(   \(AAA1 to AAA6\). AAA1 is the primary catalytic ATPase; an antiparallel coiled-coil stalk \(15 nm) Tj
T*
(   long\) projects between AAA4 and AAA5, terminating in a small globular microtubule-binding) Tj
T*
(   domain \(MTBD\). An elongated mechanical lever arm called the Buttress projects from AAA5 to) Tj
T*
(   support the stalk.) Tj
T*
(   - Intermediate, Light Intermediate, and Light Chains \(IC, LIC, LC\): Mediate motor dimerization,) Tj
T*
(   dynactin binding, and cargo attachment.) Tj
T*
(   2. The AAA+ Ring Mechanochemical Cycle:) Tj
T*
(   - In the apo \(nucleotide-free\) state, the MTBD binds tightly to the microtubule.) Tj
T*
(   - ATP binding to AAA1 induces closure of the AAA1-AAA2 cleft, propagating a conformational) Tj
T*
(   shear along the coiled-coil stalk that dramatically lowers MTBD microtubule affinity, causing) Tj
T*
(   detachment.) Tj
T*
(   - ATP hydrolysis to ADP-Pi primes the mechanical linker domain to bend into a cocked position.) Tj
T*
(   - MTBD rebinds the microtubule 8 nm toward the minus-end. Release of Pi and ADP triggers linker) Tj
T*
(   straightening, executing a powerful 8 nm power stroke pulling cargo toward the centrosome.) Tj
T*
(   3. Regulation by Dynactin and Lis1:) Tj
T*
(   - Isolated dynein is auto-inhibited in a folded 'Phi' conformation with low processivity.) Tj
T*
(   - Dynactin: A 1.2 MDa multi-protein complex containing a short filament of the actin-related) Tj
T*
(   protein Arp1 and a p150-Glued subunit. Dynactin pairs with cargo adaptor proteins \(e.g., BicD2\)) Tj
T*
(   to relieve the Phi-state, aligning two dynein dimers in parallel, increasing processive run) Tj
T*
(   lengths by 10-fold.) Tj
T*
(   - Lis1: Binds directly to the AAA+ ring, acting as a molecular clutch that prevents dynein) Tj
T*
(   detachment under heavy opposing loads \(up to 7 pN\), essential for nuclear migration during) Tj
T*
(   neurogenesis.) Tj
T*
