12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structural mechanics of the Nuclear Envelope and describe how the LINC complex connects the nucleoskeleton to the cytoskeleton.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Nuclear Envelope and the LINC Mechanotransduction Complex:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Organization of Nuclear Envelope:) Tj
T*
(   A double-membrane barrier consisting of:) Tj
T*
(   - Outer Nuclear Membrane \(ONM\): Continuous with the rough ER, studded with ribosomes.) Tj
T*
(   - Inner Nuclear Membrane \(INM\): Lined by the dense meshwork of the nuclear lamina and) Tj
T*
(   containing unique integral proteins \(Lamin B Receptor, Emerin, SUN proteins\).) Tj
T*
(   - Perinuclear Space: 30-50 nm aqueous lumen continuous with the ER lumen.) Tj
T*
(   2. The LINC Complex Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   The LINC \(Linker of Nucleoskeleton and Cytoskeleton\) complex is a mechanical bridge spanning) Tj
T*
(   both nuclear membranes:) Tj
T*
(   - SUN-Domain Proteins \(SUN1, SUN2\): Transmembrane proteins of the INM. Their N-terminal) Tj
T*
(   nucleoplasmic domains bind Lamin A/C and chromatin, while their C-terminal conserved SUN) Tj
T*
(   domains project into the perinuclear space.) Tj
T*
(   - KASH-Domain Proteins \(Nesprins 1-4\): Transmembrane proteins of the ONM. Their cytoplasmic) Tj
T*
(   domains bind actin stress fibers \(Nesprin-1/2 via calponin homology domains\), microtubules \(via) Tj
T*
(   kinesin/dynein\), and intermediate filaments \(via plectin\).) Tj
T*
(   - In the perinuclear lumen, a trimer of SUN domains binds three KASH peptides, forming a robust) Tj
T*
ET

