(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the biophysical properties and structural basis of the Titin molecular spring in muscle passive elasticity.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Titin Architecture and Molecular Spring Biophysics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Macromolecular Scale:) Tj
T*
(   Titin \(connectin\) is the largest single polypeptide known in biology \(~3.8 MDa, ~34,350 amino) Tj
T*
(   acids\), spanning half the sarcomere length \(~1.2 microns\) from the Z-disc to the M-line:) Tj
T*
(   - N-terminus is anchored in the Z-disc via interaction with telethonin \(T-cap\) and) Tj
T*
(   alpha-actinin.) Tj
T*
(   - C-terminus is anchored in the M-line, associated with obscurin and myomesin.) Tj
T*
(   2. The I-Band Elastic Region:) Tj
T*
(   The portion of titin spanning the I-band is not attached to thick filaments, acting as an) Tj
T*
(   extensible, two-stage entropic and enthalpic spring that generates muscle passive tension:) Tj
T*
(   - Tandem Immunoglobulin \(Ig\) Domains: Dozens of folded beta-sandwich Ig domains \(~100 amino) Tj
T*
(   acids each\) that unfold sequentially only under extreme pathological stretch, dissipating) Tj
T*
(   destructive tensile forces.) Tj
T*
(   - PEVK Segment: An intrinsically disordered, proline-glutamate-valine-lysine-rich entropic) Tj
T*
(   spring that extends freely during physiological muscle lengthening.) Tj
T*
(   - N2A / N2B Elements: Modulate stiffness in skeletal versus cardiac titin isoforms.) Tj
T*
(   3. Physiological Functions:) Tj
T*
(   - Centering Thick Filaments: Restores thick myosin filaments to the exact center of the) Tj
T*
(   sarcomere during relaxation, preventing sarcomeric shear distortion.) Tj
T*
(   - Passive Restoring Force: Provides passive tension resisting overstretch and recoil energy) Tj
T*
(   during diastolic ventricular filling in the heart.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
