(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the molecular mechanism of Cilia Disassembly during cell cycle entry and explain why primary cilia must be resorbed before mitosis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Molecular Mechanisms and Cell Cycle Gating of Ciliary Resorption:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Mutual Exclusivity of Cilia and Mitosis:) Tj
T*
(   The mother centriole of the centrosome functions as the basal body anchoring the primary cilium) Tj
T*
(   in G0/G1 phase. To execute mitosis, the mother centriole must be freed from the plasma) Tj
T*
(   membrane, duplicate, and migrate to opposite cellular poles to organize the bipolar mitotic) Tj
T*
(   spindle. Therefore, the primary cilium must be completely disassembled prior to mitotic entry.) Tj
T*
(   2. Molecular Disassembly Pathway:) Tj
T*
(   - Growth Factor Signaling: Upon serum restimulation, growth factors activate the Aurora A) Tj
T*
(   kinase pathway at the basal body.) Tj
T*
(   - Aurora A Activation of HDAC6: Aurora A phosphorylates and activates the tubulin deacetylase) Tj
T*
(   HDAC6. Active HDAC6 removes acetyl groups from Lys-40 of alpha-tubulin in axonemal) Tj
T*
(   microtubules, destabilizing the axonemal core.) Tj
T*
(   - Kif24 Depolymerase Activation: Phosphorylation of the kinesin-13 family member Kif24) Tj
T*
(   stimulates its ATP-dependent microtubule depolymerase activity specifically at the ciliary) Tj
T*
(   subdistal appendages.) Tj
T*
(   - Retrograde IFT Evacuation: Depolymerized axonemal fragments and ciliary membrane receptors) Tj
T*
(   are rapidly evacuated toward the cell body via retrograde dynein-2 IFT trains.) Tj
T*
(   - Plk1 Kinase Orchestration: Polo-like kinase 1 \(Plk1\) activates the pericentriolar kinase) Tj
T*
(   Nek2, triggering separation of duplicated centrioles and final uncoupling of the basal body) Tj
T*
(   from the membrane.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
