(   - Activates a cryptic splice donor site 150 bp upstream, yielding an mRNA deleted for 150) Tj
T*
(   nucleotides.) Tj
T*
(   - The resulting mutant protein, Progerin, has an internal deletion of 50 amino acids that) Tj
T*
(   removes the ZMPSTE24 endoproteolytic cleavage site!) Tj
T*
(   3. Cellular Pathology:) Tj
T*
(   Progerin undergoes farnesylation and carboxymethylation normally, but cannot undergo the final) Tj
T*
(   cleavage step. Progerin remains permanently farnesylated and membrane-bound, accumulating) Tj
T*
(   abnormally at the inner nuclear membrane. This causes:) Tj
T*
(   - Severe lobulation and nuclear envelope blebbing.) Tj
T*
(   - Loss of peripheral heterochromatin and histone H3K9me3 marks.) Tj
T*
(   - Disruption of the LINC complex, accumulation of double-strand DNA breaks, telomere attrition,) Tj
T*
(   and premature cellular senescence.) Tj
T*
(   4. Mechanism of Farnesyltransferase Inhibitors \(FTIs, e.g., Lonafarnib\):) Tj
T*
(   - Lonafarnib competitively inhibits the protein farnesyltransferase enzyme, blocking attachment) Tj
T*
(   of the farnesyl lipid tail to mutant prelamin A.) Tj
T*
(   - Without the hydrophobic anchor, unfarnesylated progerin cannot remain trapped at the inner) Tj
T*
(   nuclear membrane.) Tj
T*
(   - FTI treatment significantly restores normal nuclear morphology, reduces DNA damage signaling,) Tj
T*
(   improves cardiovascular arterial compliance, and extends survival in HGPS clinical trials.) Tj
T*
